# Git attributes that jig trace form passes to git show, so that the header of
# each hunk names the Python, bash, Rust or C function it falls in. Without them
# git names the nearest line that starts with a letter, which is often a class or
# an import, not the function that changed.
*.py diff=python
*.sh diff=bash
*.bash diff=bash
# The methods of a Rust impl block are indented, so without this rule git would
# name the impl line for a change inside any of them.
*.rs diff=rust
# A label of a C function, such as the target of a goto, starts at column 0, so
# without this rule git would name the label for a change below it.
*.c diff=cpp
*.h diff=cpp
